silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_05_glue_as_kleisli_arrow_yoneda_hom_leg_3 a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "GlueKleisliLegLambdaTaxExample" .
silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_05_glue_as_kleisli_arrow_yoneda_hom_leg_3 silm:hasExample "In 'GlueKleisliLegLambdaTax', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, JoC §11: lambda_tax: TypedLeg_taxonomy -> Mittens is the taxonomy component of the colimit cocone for D_Mittens. For the Mittens fixture, it commits TaxRow_TSN_183798 (ITIS row for Felis catus, valid, rank Species) as the taxonomy source leg of the cat. The leg is preserved separately from lambda_cls (classification), keeping the negative-regression \"Mittens = catus\" blocked." .
